<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee coop stocks record low set end-May.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee coop stocks record low set end-May.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Coffee stocks held by Brazilian cooperatives totaled only 850,395 60.5-kg bags on May 31, the lowest since records began, the National Coffee Council (CNC) said in a statement.</p>
<p>This is down from than the 981,475 bags held by cooperatives as of April 30 and also well below the 1.21 million bags held at the end of May in 1996.</p>
<p>Sales by cooperatives reached 399,065 bags in May versus 609,063 bags during April and 351,155 bags in May last year.</p>
<p>Cooperatives received 267,985 bags of coffee during the month of May against 104,011 bags delivered the previous month and 228,219 bags received in May 1996, the CNC said.</p>
<p>((-Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151))</p>
